          aria-label="Panel 2, tilt and reweight: the rate function, built from the Cramér transform of the per-server net input, gives the most likely path, which gives a tilted law Q under which the event is common (Gaussian case: Q equals N of a, 1). M runs are drawn from Q, each is weighted by dP/dQ (Gaussian case: exp of minus a X plus a squared over 2), and the estimate is the average over all runs of the weight times the indicator that the run hit A.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="ld-d2b-arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
